# Consecutive Equal Pairs Detector

## Main Goal

This code (heavily obfuscated with meaningless helper methods, dead string expressions like `"".length()`, and pointless conditionals) reads an integer **n**, then reads **n** pairs of integers. It checks whether any pair has two equal values (u == v). If **3 or more consecutive pairs** satisfy this condition, it sets a flag to "possible." At the end, it prints **"Yes"** if that flag was triggered at any point while reading the pairs, otherwise it prints **"No"**.

**Core logic (stripped of obfuscation):**
```java
int n = sc.nextInt();
int count = 0, poss = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    int u = sc.nextInt();
    int v = sc.nextInt();
    if (u == v) {
        count++;
    } else {
        count = 0;
    }
    if (count >= 3) {
        poss = 1;
    }
}
System.out.println(poss != 0 ? "Yes" : "No");
```

